{"name":"Seal Brown","hex":"#321414","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"seal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A pinniped (Pinnipedia), particularly an earless seal (true seal) or eared seal."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To hunt seals."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seal"},{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Seal brown (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Seal brown is a hair coat color of horses characterized by a near-black body color; with black points, the mane, tail and legs; but also reddish or tan areas around the eyes, muzzle, behind the elbow and in front of the stifle. The term is not to be confused with \"brown\", which is used by some breed registries to refer to either a seal brown horse or to a dark bay without the additional characteristics of seal brown."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Vesuvio_Bien_Vee_-_Paso_Fino_Bellas_Formas_National_Champion_3_Year_Old_Gelding_in_2001%3B_photo_taken_in_May_of_2006.JPG/330px-Vesuvio_Bien_Vee_-_Paso_Fino_Bellas_Formas_National_Champion_3_Year_Old_Gelding_in_2001%3B_photo_taken_in_May_of_2006.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seal_brown_(horse)","wikidata":"Q3179900"},{"title":"Seal brown","blocks":[{"text":"Seal brown is a rich dark brown color, resembling the color of the dyed fur from the fur seal."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seal_brown","wikidata":"Q612837"},{"title":"Brown","blocks":[{"text":"Brown is a color. It can be thought as a darker, typically desaturated shade of orange, and can often be produced by combining red and yellow with another color, namely blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown","wikidata":"Q47071"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Kevin_Tornado_Zlosyn_2005.jpg/330px-Kevin_Tornado_Zlosyn_2005.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Kevin_Tornado_Zlosyn_2005.jpg/330px-Kevin_Tornado_Zlosyn_2005.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The tan hair around the eyes and muzzle with a very dark body color is typical of seal brown.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKevin_Tornado_Zlosyn_2005.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Klacz_masci_brazowej.JPG/500px-Klacz_masci_brazowej.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Klacz_masci_brazowej.JPG/1280px-Klacz_masci_brazowej.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Klacz_masci_brazowej.JPG/500px-Klacz_masci_brazowej.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"This horse looks \"brown\", but the non-black lower legs give him away as a dark liver chestnut.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKlacz_masci_brazowej.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/State_fair_06_029.jpg/500px-State_fair_06_029.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/State_fair_06_029.jpg/1280px-State_fair_06_029.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm